Start the program.
Create an empty AVL tree.
Accept the number of elements from the user.
Read the elements and insert them into the AVL tree.
Calculate the height and balance factor of each node.
Check whether an LR imbalance occurs.
If an LR imbalance occurs:
Perform a left rotation on the left child.
Display the tree and its balance factors.
Perform a right rotation on the unbalanced node.
Display the final balanced tree and its balance factors.
If another type of imbalance occurs, perform the appropriate AVL rotation.
Display the final AVL tree and its inorder traversal.
Stop the program.
